        "notes": "TOXICITY IS A RELATED-NAME SOURCE: the ASPCA page read is titled Prayer Plant but gives the scientific name Calathea insignis (also listing Maranta as a common name); NC State and RHS say nothing on toxicity. Graded 0 from_knowledge_verify, as with the calathea entry. Habit bushy is a mapping from 'clumping, spreading from rhizomes'. Temperature: RHS only gives a frost-tender band (10 to 15 C minimum), NC State says cold and drafts are not tolerated; no range stored. Humidity is high on both pages but without numbers. Growth rate: not stated (RHS gives 5 to 10 years to maturity)."
